---
import {getCollection,render} from 'astro:content';import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';import {url} from '../lib/paths';
const lessons=(await getCollection('lessons')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
const targets=new Map(await Promise.all(lessons.map(async lesson=>{if(lesson.id==='collections/hashmap')return [lesson.id,'practice'] as const;const {headings}=await render(lesson);const target=headings.findLast(heading=>heading.depth===2&&/interview|exercises|practice/i.test(heading.text));return [lesson.id,target?.slug||headings.find(heading=>heading.depth===2)?.slug||'main-content'] as const})));
---
<SiteLayout title="Coding and interview practice" summary="Practise explaining behavior, tracing state changes, implementing algorithms and evaluating tradeoffs."><h2>Practice sequence</h2><ol><li>State the contract and assumptions.</li><li>Trace a small example before coding.</li><li>Implement the required behavior.</li><li>Test success, missing values, boundaries and failures.</li><li>Explain invariants, complexity and alternatives.</li></ol><h2>Implementation exercises</h2><p><a href={url('learn/collections/hashmap/#implementation')}>Implement HashMap in Java</a> includes complete source, a method walkthrough and tests. The dynamic-array, bounded-queue and LRU chapters develop further exercises. Browser simulations illustrate behavior; downloadable Java programs execute locally.</p><h2>Chapter exercises</h2>{lessons.map(l=><a class="lesson-row" href={url('learn/'+l.id+'/#'+targets.get(l.id))}><span><strong>{l.data.title}</strong><small>Worked questions, common errors and explained solutions</small></span></a>)}</SiteLayout>
